# fixedbugs, defect 2052, 2026-10-13, a function the link finds.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own calling the C library's `abs`
# without including `<stdlib.h>` built and printed 8 at exit 0, clang
# declaring the name itself where C11 declares nothing (6.5.1p2), its
# error for that ignored with `-Wall` in the header's region.
#
# FIX: `-Wimplicit-function-declaration` stays an error in the region
# (`emit/header_region.hero`'s `KEPT`), the header refused at the call's
# line 3, exit 1, and told to have `stdlib.h` named above it
# (`cli/header_order.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2052-a-header-that-calls-a-library-function-it-never-includes-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
